================================================================================
Upstream AAuth reference implementations (not licensed for redistribution)
================================================================================

The `make fetch-upstream` target clones the following repository, and
aauth/person-server.Dockerfile builds a container image from it:

  christian-posta/aauth-person-server

As of this writing that repository publishes no license, which under default
copyright means all rights are reserved by its author. It is therefore NOT
redistributed as part of this project: it is excluded by .gitignore, fetched
directly from its origin by the person running the lab, and built locally.

The same applies to christian-posta/extauth-aauth-resource and
christian-posta/aauth-full-demo, which were used during research spikes and
are likewise not included in this repository.

Anyone intending to use this lab beyond local evaluation should obtain
permission from the author of those repositories, or substitute their own
AAuth person/agent server. The AAuth Person Server is optional for the
default demo path, which signs pseudonymously.

================================================================================
Demonstration data
================================================================================

"Meridian Wealth" is a fictional firm. All brokerage figures, holdings, and
transactions are fixture data flowing through a real protocol path. No market
data, real accounts, or real orders are involved. Credentials committed to
this repository are development defaults for a self-contained local lab, not
secrets.
